IMPORT prelude

-- Boundaries and Survey Maps Act 1998 (Singapore) -- when a cadastral survey is complete and what a certified plan proves (s 4),
-- notices to clear boundary lines (s 9), boundary marks and the offence of obliterating one (ss 10, 11), surveyors' entry on land
-- (s 12), approval of survey plans and lodgment of assurance plans (s 15), correction of survey errors (s 16), correction of the
-- map (s 17), the map as conclusive evidence (s 18, with s 8 on bench marks), and the continuing offence of non-compliance (s 20).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSMA1998.txt (revised edition
-- incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, with Act 25 of 2024 (wef 1 October 2025) shown in s 2).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a landowner, a registered
-- surveyor or a court actually meets. Not encoded: appointment of the Chief Surveyor (s 3), the Chief Surveyor's general powers and
-- duties (ss 5, 6), the coordinated cadastre programme (s 7) beyond the s 7(f) declaration's effect on evidence, inspection of
-- records (s 13), deposit and certified copies (s 14), the s 19 self-help power, rules and fees (ss 21, 22), Mukim and Town
-- Subdivision boundaries (s 17(6)).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Boundaries and Survey Maps Act 1998 -- surveys, marks and maps`

§§ `4 -- when a cadastral survey is complete, and what a certified plan proves`

-- s 4(1): a cadastral survey "must not be taken to have been completed until" (a) the boundaries "have been determined by straight
-- lines"; (b) the physical boundaries have been demarcated (i) "by boundary marks or defined by approved coordinates" or (ii) "if it
-- is impossible or impracticable to do so, by reference to floors and walls"; (c) the area has been determined; (d) a lot number
-- has been assigned by the Chief Surveyor; and (e) a survey plan "has been approved by, and is filed in the office of, the Chief
-- Surveyor".
DECLARE CadastralSurvey HAS
    `boundaries determined by straight lines`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `demarcated by boundary marks or coordinates`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `marks or coordinates impossible or impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `demarcated by floors and walls`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `area determined`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `lot number assigned by the Chief Surveyor`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `plan approved and filed by the Chief Surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the survey` IS A CadastralSurvey
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the boundaries are demarcated` IF
        `the survey`'s `demarcated by boundary marks or coordinates`
    OR  (`the survey`'s `marks or coordinates impossible or impracticable` AND `the survey`'s `demarcated by floors and walls`)

GIVEN `the survey` IS A CadastralSurvey
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cadastral survey is complete` IF
        `the survey`'s `boundaries determined by straight lines`
    AND `the boundaries are demarcated` `the survey`
    AND `the survey`'s `area determined`
    AND `the survey`'s `lot number assigned by the Chief Surveyor`
    AND `the survey`'s `plan approved and filed by the Chief Surveyor`

-- s 4(2): "A certified plan is prima facie evidence of -- (a) the boundaries and boundary marks of the parcel of land ...; and
-- (b) the area and the lot number of that land." Nothing is said of who owns the land.
DECLARE PlanMatter IS ONE OF
    `the boundaries`
    `the boundary marks`
    `the area`
    `the lot number`
    `who owns the land`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A PlanMatter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certified plan is prima facie evidence of` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `who owns the land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `9 -- notice to clear a boundary line`

-- s 9(1): a survey officer may serve notice on an owner or person with an interest in land under cadastral survey "calling upon
-- that person to clear any boundary line". (2): where the person fails to carry out the work, the survey officer may cause it to
-- be carried out, and "the cost ... is recoverable from that person as a debt due to the Authority".
GIVEN `a notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN, `the work was done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clearing cost is recoverable from the person` IF
    `a notice was served` AND (NOT `the work was done`)

§§ `10, 11 -- boundary marks`

-- s 10(1): "Every owner of any land must preserve the boundary marks erected on the boundaries of the land." (2), (3): the Chief
-- Surveyor may replace or repair an injured, destroyed or removed mark and recover the costs from the owners of the lands the
-- marks serve "in any proportion that appears to the Chief Surveyor to be proper".
--
-- s 11(1): any person who "wilfully obliterates, removes or injures, without reasonable excuse" a boundary mark or survey control
-- mark "made or erected by, or under the direction of, the Chief Surveyor" commits an offence: a fine "not exceeding $1,000", and
-- a Magistrate's Court may further require payment of "3 times the cost of replacing and repairing" the mark "and of making any
-- survey rendered necessary". (2): levied as a fine. (3): if the offender "cannot be found", the Chief Surveyor may order the cost
-- to be paid "by the owners of the adjacent lands".
DECLARE MarkInterference HAS
    `acted wilfully`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `obliterated, removed or injured a mark`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `mark made under the Chief Surveyor`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a reasonable excuse`                 IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the act` IS A MarkInterference
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obliterating the mark is an offence` IF
        `the act`'s `acted wilfully`
    AND `the act`'s `obliterated, removed or injured a mark`
    AND `the act`'s `mark made under the Chief Surveyor`
    AND (NOT `the act`'s `had a reasonable excuse`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for obliterating a mark` IS 1000

GIVEN `replacement and repair cost` IS A NUMBER, `survey cost` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the further sum the court may require` IS
    3 TIMES (`replacement and repair cost` PLUS `survey cost`)

DECLARE CostBearer IS ONE OF
    `the offender`
    `the owners of the adjacent lands`

-- Inference: s 11(1) puts the multiplied sum on the convicted person; s 11(3) shifts the replacement cost to the adjacent owners
-- only where the offender "cannot be found".
GIVEN `the offender can be found` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CostBearer
DECIDE `who pays for replacing the mark` IS
    IF `the offender can be found` THEN `the offender` ELSE `the owners of the adjacent lands`

§§ `12 -- surveyors entering land`

-- s 12(1): the Chief Surveyor may authorise "any registered surveyor who has in force a practising certificate or any assistant
-- employed by the registered surveyor" to enter land, seabed, foreshore or building "at any reasonable time during the hours of
-- daylight", emplace marks, dig, and cut down obstructing trees. (2): before doing so "in respect of any land that is not a road",
-- the person "must, where practicable, give reasonable notice to the occupier". (3): must produce evidence of identity and
-- authority "if practicable, on first entering". (4): nothing "exempts any registered surveyor ... from liability for any damage".
DECLARE Entry HAS
    `authorised by the Chief Surveyor`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `surveyor holds a practising certificate`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `during daylight at a reasonable time`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the land is a road`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice was practicable`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable notice given to the occupier`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `producing identity was practicable`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `identity and authority produced`          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the entry` IS A Entry
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice to the occupier was required` IF
    (NOT `the entry`'s `the land is a road`) AND `the entry`'s `notice was practicable`

GIVEN `the entry` IS A Entry
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry complies with s 12` IF
        `the entry`'s `authorised by the Chief Surveyor`
    AND `the entry`'s `surveyor holds a practising certificate`
    AND `the entry`'s `during daylight at a reasonable time`
    AND ((NOT `notice to the occupier was required` `the entry`) OR `the entry`'s `reasonable notice given to the occupier`)
    AND ((NOT `the entry`'s `producing identity was practicable`) OR `the entry`'s `identity and authority produced`)

§§ `15 -- approval of survey plans and assurance plans`

-- s 15(2): "No assurance plan may be lodged in the Registry of Deeds or the Land Titles Registry" unless it (a) "is signed by a
-- registered surveyor and approved by the Chief Surveyor"; and (b) "bears a caution to the effect that the boundaries or dimensions
-- and areas are inconclusive".
GIVEN `signed by a registered surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved by the Chief Surveyor` IS A BOOLEAN, `bears the inconclusive caution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assurance plan may be lodged` IF
    `signed by a registered surveyor` AND `approved by the Chief Surveyor` AND `bears the inconclusive caution`

-- s 15(3): the Chief Surveyor "may refuse to approve" if (a) subdivision permission under s 12 of the Planning Act 1998 "has not
-- been obtained"; (b) "the prescribed survey fees have not been paid"; or (c) an encroachment created by the purchaser or owner of
-- the parcel being surveyed "for any relevant purpose" affects adjoining land "and the registered surveyor who signs the plan has
-- not certified that the encroachment has been resolved". (6): "relevant purpose" means a new State title, amalgamation or
-- subdivision.
DECLARE PlanApplication HAS
    `subdivision permission needed and missing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `survey fees paid`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `owner's encroachment affects adjoining land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `survey for a relevant purpose`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `surveyor certified encroachment resolved`  IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A PlanApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Chief Surveyor may refuse approval` IF
        `the application`'s `subdivision permission needed and missing`
    OR  (NOT `the application`'s `survey fees paid`)
    OR  (    `the application`'s `owner's encroachment affects adjoining land`
         AND `the application`'s `survey for a relevant purpose`
         AND (NOT `the application`'s `surveyor certified encroachment resolved`))

-- s 15(5): "Despite that a survey plan has been approved by the Chief Surveyor, it is the duty of the registered surveyor who
-- signed the survey plan to ensure that the survey plan ... [is] correct and accurate."
GIVEN `the plan was approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signing surveyor remains responsible for accuracy` IF
    TRUE

§§ `16 -- correcting errors in a cadastral survey`

-- s 16(2): "at any time after the survey plan has been deposited", the Chief Surveyor may direct the registered surveyor or licensed
-- firm to correct "at his or her or its expense" any error; (3) on failure, the Chief Surveyor may correct it and recover the cost.
-- (5): "Subsections (2) and (3) do not apply to an assurance plan."
GIVEN `the plan has been deposited` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is an assurance plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Chief Surveyor may direct a correction at the surveyor's expense` IF
    `the plan has been deposited` AND (NOT `it is an assurance plan`)

§§ `17 -- correcting the map`

-- s 17(2): no map "may be corrected, altered or added to in respect of any boundary ... except in the following cases": (a) survey
-- inaccuracy (measuring, plotting, or conversion and adjustment under s 7) -- notice to owners, objections "within one month";
-- (b) wrong boundary marks joined up, or a boundary has moved -- inquiry after one month's notice; (c) parcels properly surveyed and
-- fees paid on an assignment or demise; (d) conterminous owners "agree to an alteration" -- on "a deed or instrument being presented"
-- at the Registry; (e) an order of the General Division of the High Court, on an office copy "being served on the Chief Surveyor";
-- (f) unsurveyed subdivided parcels surveyed by the Chief Surveyor.
DECLARE MapChange IS ONE OF
    `a survey error in measuring, plotting or conversion`
    `wrong boundary marks were joined up`
    `the boundary has moved since the survey`
    `parcels properly surveyed on an assignment, fees paid`
    `neighbours agree and present a deed at the Registry`
    `neighbours agree but present no deed`
    `a High Court order served on the Chief Surveyor`
    `the Chief Surveyor surveys unsurveyed subdivided parcels`
    `an owner simply asks for a different boundary`

GIVEN `the change` IS A MapChange
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the map may be altered on this ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `neighbours agree but present no deed` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an owner simply asks for a different boundary` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 17(3): "If no objection is lodged ... within one month from the service of the notice, the Chief Surveyor must make an order for
-- the correction to be made." (4): if any objection is lodged, "the Chief Surveyor must hold an inquiry".
DECLARE NextStep IS ONE OF
    `an order for correction`
    `an inquiry`

GIVEN `an objection was lodged within one month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NextStep
DECIDE `what follows a notice of survey error` IS
    IF `an objection was lodged within one month` THEN `an inquiry` ELSE `an order for correction`

§§ `18 and 8 -- what is conclusive evidence`

-- s 18(1): every map published under the repealed Act is, "until it has been declared to be superseded under section 7(f),
-- conclusive evidence in all courts of the boundaries", subject only to s 17 orders. (2): "Upon a declaration under section 7(f),
-- every map generated from the coordinated cadastre is conclusive evidence". s 8: every bench mark "is conclusive evidence" of
-- height relative to the Singapore Height Datum. Contrast s 4(2) and s 14(4): a certified plan or certified copy is only prima facie.
DECLARE Record IS ONE OF
    `a map published under the repealed Act`
    `a map generated from the coordinated cadastre`
    `a certified plan`
    `a bench mark`

GIVEN `the record` IS A Record, `the s 7(f) declaration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record is conclusive evidence` IF
    CONSIDER `the record`
    WHEN `a map published under the repealed Act` THEN NOT `the s 7(f) declaration has been made`
    WHEN `a map generated from the coordinated cadastre` THEN `the s 7(f) declaration has been made`
    WHEN `a certified plan` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a bench mark` THEN TRUE

§§ `20 -- non-compliance with an order or notice`

-- s 20: any person "being legally bound to comply with any order under this Act, or with the requisition contained in any notice
-- ... wilfully refuses, or without reasonable excuse neglects, to comply" commits an offence: a fine "not exceeding $100 for every
-- day or part of every day during which the refusal or neglect continues after conviction".
GIVEN `legally bound to comply` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully refused` IS A BOOLEAN, `neglected` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `non-compliance is an offence` IF
        `legally bound to comply`
    AND (`wilfully refused` OR (`neglected` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)))

-- "every day or part of every day" -- the caller counts a part day as a day.
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine for non-compliance` IS
    100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
